  "id": "theslip",
  "note": "THE SLIP — the fence on Lever Lane that nobody signposts.\n\nThe tile's prose: a narrow frontage between two wider ones, no sign at all, a good steel door\n(steel core, three hinges, a spyhole at the height of a short woman's eye) and a window bricked down\nto a slot glazed with wire glass. People who need to find it find it.\n\nSo the street face is a narrow brick bay standing forward of a plainer, wider block behind it, and\nthe bay carries only the door, the slot and a lamp. There is no lettering anywhere on the building,\nwhich is the one thing on Lever Lane that tells you what it is. The flanks are blank brick with a\ndownpipe; the back is a yard door and bins.\n\nIt stands in for the `slipback` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_brick",
  "replaces": "slipback",
